From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] mips: jz47xx: x2600: DDR parameters by the SoC ID in
 the eFuse

The X2600 comes in variants with different DDR dies in the package:
the AD5X ships with the X2600H (512 MiB DDR3L) and the X2600E (256 MiB
DDR3). The SPL always set up the X2600H's DDR, so on an X2600E its DDR
test failed.

Read the SoC info from the eFuse as Ingenic's check_socid() does, build
the DDR ID from it and pick the matching table: the X2600H's as before,
the X2600E's and the X2600N's as the 2025 stock SPL carries them. With
no SoC info in the eFuse the X2600H's table stays the choice.

With 256 MiB, test only the address lines the DDR has, and leave the
second bank (mem=256M@0x30000000) off the kernel command line, in the
SPL and in U-Boot proper, as the stock SPL does.

Signed-off-by: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
